user_prompt_template:
UPSTREAM TUTORIAL FRAMING:
{upstream_system_architecture}

PROJECT CONTEXT:
Tutorial Request: {topic}
Skill Level: {skill_level}
Tutorial Type: {tutorial_type}
Stack: {stack}
Platform: {platform}
Constraints: {constraints}
Additional Context: {context}

Research the factual foundation for this tutorial. Cover every module in the upstream framing. Aim for 12–25 facts, 5–10 common errors, 6–12 key commands, and 5–10 references — scaled to the number of modules.

Before finalising each fact, ask: could a developer verify this against official docs or a terminal? If not, lower its confidence or remove it.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "research_summary": "3–5 sentences: the stack's current state as it affects this tutorial — what is stable, what is version-sensitive, and where learners most often get stuck",
  "facts": [
    {{
      "fact_id": "fact-01",
      "claim": "One specific, verifiable statement about the stack — exact enough to write a step against",
      "category": "version | command | configuration | gotcha | concept | security | compatibility",
      "applies_to_modules": ["domain-01"],
      "confidence": "high | medium | low",
      "source_hint": "Where this is documented — e.g. 'Next.js docs — App Router → Server Components'"
    }}
  ],
  "version_baselines": [
    {{
      "tool": "Tool or runtime name",
      "minimum_version": "Minimum or recommended version, with the verification command",
      "notes": "Why this baseline matters for this tutorial — what breaks below it"
    }}
  ],
  "common_errors": [
    {{
      "symptom": "What the learner sees — exact error message text where stable, otherwise the observable behavior",
      "cause": "The actual mechanism behind it",
      "fix": "The concrete fix — file, field, command",
      "applies_to_modules": ["domain-01"]
    }}
  ],
  "key_commands": [
    {{
      "command": "Copy-pasteable command",
      "run_from": "Where to run it — e.g. 'project root', 'any terminal'",
      "purpose": "What it does in this tutorial",
      "expected_output": "What success looks like — output string or observable result",
      "applies_to_modules": ["domain-01"]
    }}
  ],
  "reference_links": [
    {{
      "title": "Official doc name and section",
      "url": "Canonical URL — site root or stable section path",
      "why": "What the learner or writer uses it for"
    }}
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Each low-confidence fact restated as a verification task — e.g. 'Verify the current default region list in `fly platform regions` before writing step 2'"
  ]
}}
